\cf1\b\fs32 New Features\cf0\b0\fs20\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720\fs24 Support for Windows 8 32/64-bit\cf2\f2\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1800\cf0\f0 External Trigger source can know be set to 'Software Trigger' in order for the board to ignore any physical trigger applied to the board.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Added support for Acq Status \f3\fs20 CORACQ_VAL_SIGNAL_PIXEL_CLK_1_PRESENT, CORACQ_VAL_SIGNAL_PIXEL_CLK_2_PRESENT, CORACQ_VAL_SIGNAL_PIXEL_CLK_3_PRESENT, CORACQ_VAL_SIGNAL_PIXEL_CLK_ALL_PRESENT\f0\fs24\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1440\cf2\f2\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li720\cf0\f0\fs20\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\cf1\b\fs32 Fixes\ul\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 Linescan mode + FFC enabled: With parallel taps, if line merging was enabled, the FFC would not work. Starting with this driver, line merging is turned off when selecting Linescan mode + FFC enabled.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Driver will now detect disconnect/connect of 2nd Camera Link cable when applicable. The status CORACQ_VAL_SIGNAL_PIXEL_CLK_ALL_PRESENT and Pixel Clock Events Present/Absent will reflect the combination of all required pixel clocks based on the Camera Link Configuration selected.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sb40\sa20\tx360\tx720 Added default Shaft Encoder Debouncer of 100nsec. Without any debouncer, some opto-coupler parts could generate false trigger detections at high speed rates.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Buffer host PC time stamp would be ' 0' except for 1st frame of a sequence when EXT_TRIGGER_FRAME_COUNT > 1.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Random buffer host PC time stamp = 0 when grabbing from dual channel camera.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Randomly, after loading line scan CCF file, and enabling external trigger delay of at least 1 line, the 1st external frame trigger received could be dropped.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Improved prevention of BSOD upon reset of the board that can occur in some computers. Solution needs SaperaLT 7.40 and up.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Upon opening serial port, the HW Fifo was not reset causing any data in th Fifo to be transfered to the user application. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}External Frame Trigger Delay in usec or Ext Line Trigger/Shaft Encoder was not grabbing anything if a drop count was specified. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Removed CAPs CORACQ_VAL_TIME_BASE_SHAFT_ENCODER from EXT_TRIGGER_DELAY_TIME_BASE. Was never supported. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Fixed support for time stamp in msec. It would return values in usec.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}PoCL clock detection timeout was hardcoded to 2 seconds, below the Camera Link specification of 3 seconds. \tab\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}PoCL state is now persistent when closing/opening SaperaLT application.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Serial port would get reset when opening a SaperaLT application.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Buffer Timestamp in usec could randomly be inaccurate when using 10 tap FPGA.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Virtual Frame Trigger when used along with a trigger delay and a shaft encoder drop count could become unstable when modifying the frame count per external frame trigger.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx720\cf1\fs32\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\sl240\slmult0\b Backward Compatibility\b0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult0\tx720\cf2\f1\fs20\'b7\tab\f0\fs24 Compatible with Sapera LT version 5.20 and later (XP), 6.02 and later (Windows 7),\line 6.02 and later (Windows 8 64-bit), 7.30 and later (Windows 8 32-bit).\par
\f1\fs20\'b7\tab\f0\fs24 For Wow64 driver under 64-bit OS,  compatible with Sapera LT version \cf0 7.11.02.1057\cf2\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li720\sl240\slmult0\tx720\fs20\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\cf1\b\fs32 Notes\cf0\b0\fs20\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720\fs24 Cropping width must be a multiple of 16 pixels.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Hactive must be a multiple of 16 pixels/taps with multi-segmented tap cameras.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Serial ports are only available once a Sapera application has started/executed. This will be the case in most instances as Device Manager runs on every bootup. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}4 taps of 8 bits with alternated taps and Camera Link configuration "two bases" is not supported.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}External Trigger Acquisition Callback \par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li1440\tx720 Line scan: edge and level trigger\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Area scan: edge trigger only\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720 The LUT must not be change/set while grabbing.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Vertical flip, Horizontal flip and cropping is not supported for 10 taps camera.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Horizontal flip is not support for dual channel camera and for 2 alternated taps 10 or 12 bits camera.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}For 10 taps camera, to maximize the bandwidth, do not crop horizontally and use a multiple of 8 lines.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}In variable frame length, the external trigger must be inactive for at least one line.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Monochrome camera with 8 taps alternated are not supported.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}To optimize transfer bandwidth, parallel taps of 2, 4, 8 and 10 taps are automatically merged if the following conditions are met\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li1440\tx720 No horizontal or vertical flipping is requested\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}All tap directions are from top to bottom\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}No horizontal cropping of incoming image is requested\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}If in Linescan mode, FFC is not enabled\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li720\tx720\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li720\tx720\tab\ul  \b For 2, 4 and 8 taps parallel\par
\ulnone\b0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx720\tab\ul Line length of 2K and less:\ulnone  line merging will be done on 2, 4 or 8 lines depending on the line length in pixels. If the number of vertical lines to acquire is not a multiple of the number of lines to merge, no merging will be done.\line\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li720\tx720\par
\tab Line Length:\tab 0 - 800 : 4 lines\line\tab\tab 801 - 1024 : 2 lines\line\tab\tab 1025 - 2048 : 8 lines \par
\line\ul Line length multiple of 2K\ulnone : No merging.\par
\line\ul Line length > 2K:\ulnone  number of lines merged = 2048 / (Line Length % 2048), maximum of 8 lines. If number of vertical lines to acquire is not a\line multiple of the number of lines to merge, the driver will try to merge less lines.\par
\par
\tab\ul\b For 10 taps parallel:\ulnone\b0  number of lines merged = 65536 / Line Length, maximum of 255 lines. If number of vertical lines to acquire is not a\line multiple of the number of lines to merge, the driver will try to merge less lines.\ul\b\par
\ulnone\b0\tab\line       \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li1440\tx720\ul\b Note:\ulnone\b0  Line merging imposes constraint on the number of vertical lines that must be a multiple of the number of lines merged. This can be an issue when acquiring variable frame length images. If transfer bandwidth is not an issue, the CORXFER_PRM_LINE_MERGING can be used to turn off the automatic line merging of parallel taps.\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720 In 3-tap parallel configuration, the DataValid signal is always active, and cannot be de-activated. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The buffer parameter CORBUFFER_PRM_SPACE_USED is updated only if the transfer event 'End of Frame' is registered.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The buffer state CORBUFFER_VAL_STATE_OVERFLOW is set only if the transfer event 'End of Frame' is registered.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The external frame trigger (in linescan) when set to acquire on a level high or low, will only start acquisition when an edge, rising or falling respectively, is detected.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}When acquiring from 2 bayer sources simultaneously, it is recommended to create 3 or more internal buffers per input in order to avoid losing frames. \line Also, note that there is only one bayer to RGB converter on the board, so images are converted in a serial fashion.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sb40\sa20\tx360\tx720 Removed HS80 specific firmware ("\b\f4\fs20 One Full Camera Link Input with Flat Field Correction\b0  (FFC), optimized for use with the Teledyne DALSA HS-80 camera.\f0\fs24 "). The optimization has been integrated into the standard Full FPGA. \par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1440 Dual Bayer firmware supports serial port speed up to 115200 baud and supports a minimum of 4 pixels for the physical LVAL.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720 Software Trigger is not available if an external trigger delay other than 0 is specified and the external trigger source is not set to 'Software Trigger'.\fs20\par
\fs24{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}When Host PC time stamp is set to  ACQ - End of Frame, it's possible for some time stamps to return '0' because of inversion of events between ACQ - End of Frame and XFER - End of Frame.\fs20\par
\fs24{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible PC crash when acquiring with a high data and frame rate.\fs20\par
\fs24{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible missing end of frame with 8 taps parallel camera configuration and line length >= 4k. Problem would depend on number of lines acquired.\fs20\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li360\par
